# Token efficiency (every prompt)

## Conversation
- Prefer a **new chat** for a new screen/topic; do not drag unrelated prior module context.
- Answer the **latest user ask only** — no full history restatement or long “plan then do” essays.
- If the ask is clear, proceed; ask **at most one** clarifying question when blocked.

## Scope
- Touch **only** files needed for the ask. No drive-by refactors or unrelated modules.
- Read/search the **smallest** set of files. Do not scan the whole codebase for a one-screen fix.
- Prefer paths the user names (controller / view / route).

## Output
- **Short replies**: bullets over paragraphs; no preamble.
- Show changed blocks / commit list — not full-file dumps.
- **Skip** canvases, architecture essays, WhatsApp writeups, and new markdown docs **unless explicitly asked**.
- Do not narrate tool usage or repeat the task back.

## Tools
- Batch independent reads; avoid re-reading the same large file.
- No broad explore agents for small UI/logic fixes.
- Prefer pasted error/URL/text over screenshot analysis when both exist.
- Smoke/lint **only** touched paths when risk warrants it — no full-suite by default.

## Git
- Commit **only** when the user asks. Prefer small screen-wise commits.
- Do not commit cache, sessions, logs, `assets.zip`, or throwaway smoke screenshots unless asked.

## Still required
- Smallest correct CI3 diff; match existing style.
- No business-logic / API / schema / UI behavior change unless the user explicitly requests it.
